  <section class="individual bg-darkblue pb-3 pt-5">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;">
            <h3 class="centered"><span class="username">Chamilka</span>, You Are The <span class="archetype">Outlaw</span> - <span class="text-orange">And This Is What It Means...</span></h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/it-means.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>The Outlaw archetype is notorious, free-minded, and free-spirited... Nothing stands in your, way and nothing controls your desires. You are the true representation of what it really means to be the captain of your own ship. As an Outlaw, <span class="text-orange">accountability to others</span> makes you feel trapped, and that's why you prefer to answer to no one.</p>
              <p>Truth be told, the Outlaw archetype is not merely one-dimensional. It has many different sides and faces, and as we progress through this Archetypal Introduction, you'll begin to understand what I mean. But before we proceed, please do so with with an open mind, and a willing heart.</p>
              <p>The Outlaw archetype is one that tends to go against the grain. You're often challenging the rules and conventions of <span class="text-orange">societal expectations</span> and governmental control. You're able to speak with conviction about the things that you're passionate about, and that often includes ultimate freedom and rebelling against authority.</p>
              <p>But what really sets you apart is your passion for charitable causes and movements... Whether it's providing stray animals with a home, raising orphans, or building shelters in struggling areas. The Outlaw archetype, unlike other archetypes, is one that talks the talk, and walks the walk. Your actions and decisions are often reflective of and <span class="text-orange">juxtapose to your personal beliefs</span>.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>That seems to spring from your profound connection to people and things that are lost and forgotten... A connection that ignites a spark in you to create massive change in society - to actualize your vision of a new world. Despite your edgy and intense mannerisms, deep down, you're actually someone who's both passionate and compassionate.</p>
          <p>People find themselves drawn to you because of your thought-provoking insights that spur deep, thoughtful conversations. That's because you're always on high alert when it comes to social issues, injustice, inequality, or practically anything that screams unfairness.</p>
          <p>You do have vigilante tendencies, <span class="username"></span>... If given the chance to take matters into your own hands, you would not blink twice. That, however, sometimes lands you into trouble.</p>
          <p>You are the defender of the weak; the one to stand up against bullies, to restore power to the people, and bring justice to those who stole it from them. As an Outlaw, you despise systems and all that's attached to it - forming the foundation of your <span class="text-orange">rebel heart</span>, and your formidable spirit.</p>
          <p>Your stance is grounded with conviction, and you have no qualms with putting naysayers in their place. And that conviction is articulated with your passion for the helpless and the hopeless.</p>
          <p>In more ways than one, you have a strong sense of mission - an <span class="text-orange">agent of change</span>, if you will. That stems from your firm belief in the fact that everyone is born equal. And you will do whatever it takes to make it so. </p>
          <p>The Outlaw archetype has a deep-seated connection to the feeble and forgotten. You represent their voice, as well as the need for change in the world.</p>
          <p>But we'll discuss that in greater detail as we progress through this Archetypal Introduction.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual text-left pb-3 pt-5">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;" class="long-title">
            <h3 class="centered">As A <span class="archetype">Outlaw</span>, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Hidden Qualities, Unknown Tendencies,<br>And Positive Attributes</span> That You Wouldn't Expect</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4">
              <img src="../assets/images/abilities.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>Being a rebellious character, you tend to have a charismatic look about yourself, drawing followers in part because you can read other people’s emotions very well. You are inherently sensitive to other people and often the one to bring new experiences to those around you, and for this reason, though you may make enemies from time to time, you also have loyal friends that suit your extroversion.</p>
              <p>Egocentric</p>
              <p>Unsurprisingly, you have a tendency to look at the world from your perspective and prioritize yourself as a result. Though you are aware that you can’t accomplish everything alone, the reality is that your worldview can sometimes be imposed upon others. This means that while you are steadfast in your principles, you can be seen as somewhat of a tyrant in the way you act.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>As an Outlaw, you have a <span class="text-orange">rational mind</span> that actually thinks for itself. You pride yourself in this particular quality, because it is the very tool that allows you to solve problems. This does mean that you offer a lot less room for doubt, but this is only necessary because an Outlaw expects results above all else. With this quality, you are essentially a force of thought and reason.</p>
          <p>Turbulent</p>
          <p>Finally, as a Turbulent person, you are often driven and <span class="text-orange">hungry for self-improvement</span>. You want to bring yourself to your very best each time, and you are always committed to making sure that you serve your cause excellently. However, this can also cause you to be quite uncertain and even worried that you might not be doing hard enough, to the point where your confidence can be damaged.</p>
          <p>That being said, there’s more about your potential than you understand at this juncture, <span class="username"></span>. </p>
          <p>With your hidden qualities in full view, it is time for you to know what your strengths are and how you can better use them...</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-1" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(1,2)">Show Me Now</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual bg-darkblue pb-3 pt-5" id="step2">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;" class="long-title">
            <h3 class="centered">As A Outlaw, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Hidden Strengths And<br>Positive Attributes</span> That You Wouldn't Expect</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/abilities-2.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>As an Outlaw, you are naturally daring. Thrill runs in your veins and you will do everything you can to satisfy it. For you, thrill is the truest form of personal freedom and the gateway to improvement. Anything less than excitement leads to stagnation and decay.</p>
              <p>This natural propensity to seek what people haven’t tried yet allows you to constantly think outside the limits of other archetypes. You are, therefore, the person everyone turns to for fun, novelty and having <span class="text-orange">creative solutions for difficult problems</span>. That being said, this may only come after settling some misunderstanding others might have about your true nature.</p>
              <p>Of course, although this is a strength, you should be aware that not everyone is going to be able to keep up. Some might think that you’re risking yourself too much, but to you, such sentiments are only fuel. As such, you are a limit-breaking daredevil.</p>
              <p>By definition, an Outlaw has to be decisive. After all, how are you going to be able to break the rules if you are constantly giving in to hesitation? You are aware that life has an element of luck and destiny to it, and that sometimes, exploiting them means letting go of your personal limiters.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Not only are you decisive, you also tend to take risky choices from time to time. In fact, you may sometimes do so simply because you want to deal with the hesitation you’re already feeling deep down. This naturally means that there is a side of you that’s <span class="text-orange">whimsical and willing to explore</span>.</p>
          <p>And due to your extroverted nature, you might often argue with other people about the merits of your decision. You are proud and hardly feel any regret in any choice you make. This doesn’t mean you don’t think things through either, but when you’re done, nothing can stop you.</p>
          <p>And as expected of any Outlaw, you are always focused on criticizing things. Sometimes, you have a habit of simply taking the other side in arguments simply because you want to challenge the limits of the other position. As a result of your persistent and rather aggressive way of <span class="text-orange">looking for the truth</span>, you often see things most people miss.</p>
          <p>This fine capacity for rationality makes you an asset for any person who is able to see the products of your brilliance. Your ability to explore means you are never cut short on options, despite other archetypes giving up under similar circumstances. </p>
          <p>Similarly, you also have a habit of improving yourself in unique and inventive ways. When you’re facing a gap in your skill set, for example, you tend to fill it with even better alternatives. This results in you being able to compete with others despite having far less experience or seniority than them. </p>
          <p>Add to that, another crucial trait of the Outlaw that stems from their turbulence and rationality is their depth. For you, you refuse to only think of things on the surface level. If you have a strategy, you will think not only about the individual methods you use to implement such strategies, but even the theory and ethics of said strategies.</p>
          <p>Not only that, you also have a deep grasp of who you really are as a human being. You are full of purpose that only you can explain to yourself, which means you end up hesitating a lot less. This self-wisdom attracts people to your side as they are eager to learn how you managed to get to such a stage in your life.</p>
          <p>Lastly, you are ever so <span class="text-orange">perceptive and observant</span> of your current surroundings. Your deep understanding of the world means that you will pursue friendships for goals that even other people can’t easily understand. You can foresee danger to a limited degree because you immerse yourself in the world’s ways and refuse to simply take for granted common wisdom. Nothing is sacred to you-- on the contrary, everything becomes sacred once you understand them.</p>
          <p>Now that you’re acquainted with your strengths, dear <span class="username"></span>, it is time for you to know how you can exercise them in various aspects of your life. </p>
          <p>For now, let’s start with one that strikes a chord: your romantic relationships.</p>

        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-2" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(2,3)">Show Me Now</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual text-left pb-3 pt-5" id="step3">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;" class="long-title">
            <h3 class="centered">As A Outlaw, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Relationship Qualities</span> That Are Within You</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4">
              <img src="../assets/images/relationship.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>Due to your rational nature, you tend to be very understanding of other people. Whereas other archetypes tend to be impatient and aggressive, you are inclined to reason and understanding.</p>
              <p>When you are in a relationship, this tendency will bring reassurance. As such, likely won’t focus too much on a person’s faults in a relationship. You <span class="text-orange">won’t try to collect grievances</span> to get back at them at a later time, but will instead keep the relationship steady.</p>
              <p>Given this, you are likely to encourage your partner and give them strength in their most trying time. Though you are an Outlaw, you will know better than to get in the way of your partner who is also set on their dreams and objectives.</p>
              <p>This means that you, surprisingly, know the meaning of compromise deep down. This may not surface itself as often as your partner would like, but they know that when they are backed into a corner, you will ultimately come through for them when they really need it most.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Of course, despite this surprising knack for knowing other people and compromising for them, it may still be buried in the form of misgivings, or otherwise pushing your own agenda until the relationship is strained. </p>
          <p>This can still result in arguments between you two from time to time, and this will naturally push you to be more assertive of your own agenda. Although you ultimately will <span class="text-orange">resolve arguments</span> in the end, you should still expect to see some fights here and there over the course of your relationship.</p>
          <p>As such, you should develop your natural capacity for understanding even further to make the relationship even more harmonious. When in love, look beyond your own individuality so that you can pursue even greater things with your significant other. Have your disagreements, but maintain your capacity for understanding and the relationship will last.</p>
          <hr class="dashed">
          <p>Looking at the core qualities of your archetype, we’ll see an Outlaw whose self-pride can definitely get in the way of a harmonious relationship. On the one hand, you are assertive enough to make sure you aren’t dominated, but this could mean a less harmonious relationship.</p>
          <p>Such trait often manifests in your likelihood to gain criticism for your own actions. The one thing you always manifest is a desire to make your will known, and to that end, you aren’t as scared of having an equal who might have opposing views to your own. They may, however, see you as somewhat of a liability due to your own <span class="text-orange">boundless egotism</span>.</p>
          <p>This may extend further to a degree, in that your partner’s friends may not just like your attitude. Your ideas themselves will be certainly beyond reproach, given that you are a highly rational person, but your eccentricities will certainly trigger alarm bells from plenty of naysayers who might think you’re too arrogant for your own good.</p>
          <p>Now, let there be no mistake: pride in and of itself isn’t exactly a bad thing. There is no shame in being proud of who you are and what you do. On the contrary, pride is even necessary in your case since it is the lifeblood of your entire personality. Without pride, the Outlaw cannot exist.</p>
          <p>However, if you do not take the time to at least learn other people’s points of view and their merits, the Outlaw will not thrive for long either. The essence of a strong relationship will always be compromise between both sides. To assert your own pride repeatedly will give your partner the impression that you can’t make relationships work.</p>
          <p>To this end, you must first learn to engage with others without putting them off before getting into relationships, as doing so will allow you to actually adapt to them. Remember that romantic relationships are a team effort: <span class="text-orange">you cannot succeed on your own</span>.</p>
          <p>As you know, however, the Outlaw is not just about romance and love. Indeed, there’s another aspect in your life where you can apply yourself, <span class="username"></span>. </p>
          <p>Without further ado, it’s time to see where you can take yourself in your career.</p>

        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-3" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(3,4)">Show Me Now</a>
        </div>
