  </section>

  <section class="individual bg-darkblue pb-3 pt-5" id="step4">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;">
            <h3 class="centered">As A <span class="archetype">Outlaw</span>, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Potential Career Paths</span></h3>
          </div>
          <p>Generally, the Outlaw is a combination of extroversion, egocentrism, rationality, and turbulence. This makes up for strong career paths in relation to arts, academics and politics. With their argumentative nature, Outlaws will thrive in these areas. And while these are suggestive of what you can pursue with your strengths, know that you should never limit yourself to them.</p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/writer-outlaw.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Professor/Writer</h5>
              <p>With their uniqueness, Outlaws are best suited as professors/writers. Because they have the natural knack to create and challenge ideas, they’ll find it natural to be part of the academic tradition.</p>
              <p>As an Outlaw, your goal in life is to improve society in a way that isn’t exactly conventional: you wish to improve it from the inside by questioning certain concepts to help improve everyone around you.</p>
              <p>In doing so, some will naturally view you as just that-- an Outlaw. However, what they don’t understand is that plenty of other people have walked in your direction, and through their guidance, they improved society.</p>
              <p>For instance, Socrates was considered by many Athenians to be an outlaw. What he did was question deeply held values like justice, love, bravery, truth, reason, even the laws and the gods. But in doing so, we are reminded that he was only improving his home city of Athens by being the “gadfly” that constantly spurred it to activity. Rather than letting his home decay, he forced his people to question themselves.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>And it is by the example of this old man that an entire field came to be so many years later: philosophy. The academics now have a similar goal-- to find ways to improve society, even if it means questioning age-old traditions, as the ultimate goal of humanity is to seek progress. Your part in this regard is highly crucial due to your nature.</p>

          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/artist-outlaw.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Artist</h5>
              <p>Outlaws are masters of self-expression and are willing to show their opinions and ideas in unconventional ways. It’s therefore unsurprising that the art industry regularly welcomes people with their disposition.</p>
              <p>In fact, the best part about artistry is that it is full of possibilities. From just turning your feelings into tangible art, or expressing the anger or joy of an entire culture, you will never run out of thoughts to express.</p>
              <p>Due in part to your turbulent personality, you will often infuse intellectual ideas of equality and freedom with the free flowing, passionate application of the brush. Your images will be full of life and meaning.</p>
              <p>That being said, since you have an eccentric way of expressing yourself, you may have to contend with some disagreements both from fellow artists and those trying to understand your work.</p>
              <p>For instance, you may be asked in conferences to explain your work in greater detail so as to enlighten the public. The images you’ll be using will be as complex as your thoughts, so prepare for arguments!</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>In exchange for these little inconveniences, however, you will nevertheless enjoy the fact that you will be held back by nearly no one for the most part. As an artist, life itself is but a canvas waiting to be filled with inspiration and ideas. If you’re looking to express yourself without limit, this is where you can go.</p>

          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/politician-outlaw.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Politician</h5>
              <p>As ironic as it sounds, Outlaws make for good politicians. This is because politics is all about shaping the world around you. With the right policies and moves, you can guide your community to your vision. You can improve scientific or cultural literacy, and even the standard of life of your constituents! Politics allows you to help others in so many ways that it’s basically endless.</p>
              <p>You will also notice, however, that politics also forces you to work with certain constraints. For example, the laws of the land will tell you what you can and cannot do as a politician. These constraints are in place to make sure that no one can usurp the will of the people who installed them into power.</p>
              <p>You will also need to work with businessmen and other powerful people to bring about certain reforms or improvements to your community. This means making deals and constantly coming to an equitable ground between community and business interests.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Lastly, you will also need to work with your constituents. Speaking to them publicly will help you connect with them on a tangible level, while listening to their concerns will help you figure out the problematic areas of your community as well as how to address them. These collective constraints will naturally temper your own selfishness, making politics the ideal ground for self-learning.</p>
          <p>In other words, by helping others, you will ultimately be helping yourself develop into a better person for others. If you seek mutual improvement, politics is where you want to be.</p>
          <p>But while your career prospects certainly glimmer with the hope of prosperity, there are uncomfortable truths about yourself that you will need to face. The first of which will be no more comforting, <span class="username"></span>, and it is this...</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-4" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(4,5)">Show Me Now</a>
